{
  "id": "ss.terrain.tunnel",
  "name": "Tunnel mouth (SS)",
  "description": "Shape Survivors set dressing: a hole dug up through the field from below, and the same hole caved in. The spoil is heaped highest on the near lip where it was pushed out, and it is warm turned earth rather than the ruins' purple stone — the one ring on this ground that means dug, not built. Drawn at the crater tilt the pheromone vent uses, so a mouth cut into open flats and one cut into a burrow chamber read as the same object.\n\nThe rim is built in banded slopes rather than as one flat ellipse, and every band takes its side from one light, up-screen: the far bank's crest is lit (`bank_lit`) and the near bank's outer slope falls into shadow (`bank_shade`); inside the lip that reverses, because the wall you can see into a tilted hole is the far one and it faces away from the light (`wall_shade`), while the near lip's crest catches it on the turn as a thin bright line (`rim_lit`). `lip_edge` is the hard ink line the ground breaks on, drawn over the throat so the hole keeps its edge however far the thing inside it opens.\n\nWhat is inside is two used documents, and they are used rather than inlined so that the mouth can move each as one part: `ss.lib.tunnel-gullet` is the throat, the dark it pools into and four rings of muscle down it, and `ss.lib.tunnel-teeth` is the ring of fourteen husk points set into the lip. Together they are what the three clips move — `idle` is the thing breathing, `sense` is it opening on something that came close, and `swallow` is it shutting on whatever stepped in. The teeth are the only warning the object gives: nothing announces a tunnel, and a mouth that takes a bite out of whoever drops through it has to say so before they do.\n\nThe `filled` variant is what a spent tunnel leaves: the heap gone back down the hole, domed and paler than the ground it came out of, broken into clods on top and sunk away from the lip where it settled.",
