    "sense": {
      "description": "Something came close. Read against `idle` rather than on its own, and different from it on three counts at once, because one would not carry across a field: it is a third faster, it sits open at its narrowest wider than the idle ever gets, and the ring of teeth rocks a couple of degrees either way — a twist no other state has, and the thing that says the mouth is working rather than breathing. It loops for as long as whatever tripped it stays near. The step up out of `idle` is meant to be seen: that snap is the whole tell, since nothing else about a tunnel announces itself.",
